    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e520f785_4d7ac7e4",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 181,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T21:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we really want this to be an optional function? Shouldn\u0027t we add this to all TCPC implementations?\n\nThe TCPMv2 calls into this function and expects some action, if most TCPCs don\u0027t implement this, then what should happen?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 180,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 181,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "3c367a2512a9494016756d36b67c8c320c92e18d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e8d54ab_61205d6d",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 181,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T23:11:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the old code didn\u0027t expect it to set the value.  It only set the cached rp and called it a day.  Since the old code didn\u0027t do it, I didn\u0027t want to sign everyone up if their system was working as it was already implemented. The code is designed to be just like it was before for those that do not have this and that would make the change backward compatible.",
      "parentUuid": "e520f785_4d7ac7e4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 180,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 181,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "3c367a2512a9494016756d36b67c8c320c92e18d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10d99b77_fd4dd0ea",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 222,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T21:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this isn\u0027t true for 3 of the TCPC drivers. It actually Sets the RP value synchronously.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 222,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 222,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "3c367a2512a9494016756d36b67c8c320c92e18d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f4138092_24d4fa34",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 222,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T23:11:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "and maybe those 3 would not need to have this change if they implemented set_rp_value.  I think \"Set\" seems misleading.",
      "parentUuid": "10d99b77_fd4dd0ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 222,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 222,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "3c367a2512a9494016756d36b67c8c320c92e18d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e09fd8c_5b9840b3",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T21:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we need to figure out what our consistent interface it for setting Rp value and CC lines and if they are cached/asychronous and when they are synchronous (and which functions are truly optional)\n\nOnce the interface is defined, then we need to ensure that all of the TCPC drivers work with that interface.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "3c367a2512a9494016756d36b67c8c320c92e18d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d4ee39b_f62ce453",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T21:56:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Personally, I lean towards allowing asynchronous calls to cache a new Rp value, but only allowing the PD task to actually set that new value in the TCPC register since it knows the times it\u0027s allowed to set Rp for either the implicit contract or collision avoidance.",
      "parentUuid": "4e09fd8c_5b9840b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "3c367a2512a9494016756d36b67c8c320c92e18d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97d6fb29_448371b4",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_tcpm.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T23:11:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current fall back it to work as it currently is before the CL.  Thus if a TCPC driver used to work it should continue to work.  I favored adding set_rp_value over forcing the use of set_cc because I wanted to know the Rp value was the only one that would possibly change.",
      "parentUuid": "4e09fd8c_5b9840b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 229,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 248,
        "endChar": 35
